---
// Help & support — the published contact information App Store Review
// Guideline 1.2 asks of an app with user-generated content, and the page
// the app's Account screen links as "Help & support" (issue #60).
//
// It says three things a reviewer and a reader both look for: how to reach a
// person, how to report abuse from inside the app, and how fast a report is
// acted on. The 24-hour commitment is for **our** homeserver only; a report
// made on someone else's goes to them, and the page says so rather than
// promising for a server we do not run.
//
// **The address must receive mail before this ships.** `supermessage.dev` has
// no MX records (see privacy.astro's header), so the address is on
// superjackfruit.com, which routes to Google Workspace. `support@` must exist
// there as a mailbox or alias; a support page whose address bounces is worse
// than none.
//
// The head and styles are lifted from privacy.astro deliberately, so the
// compliance pages cannot drift apart visually.
import '../styles/tokens.css';
import ShareMeta from '../components/ShareMeta.astro';

const title = 'Help & support — supermessage';
const description =
  'How to reach the people behind supermessage, and how to report abuse or block someone.';

const updated = '27 September 2026';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <ShareMeta title={title} description={description} />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400;12..96,600;12..96,800&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --display: 'Bricolage Grotesque', 'Trebuchet MS', sans-serif;
        --body: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--color-surface-sunken);
        color: var(--color-content);
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      main {
        max-width: 68ch;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 48px 24px 96px;
      }

      a { color: var(--color-accent); }

      h1 {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 44px);
        line-height: 1.1;
        margin: 0 0 8px;
      }

      h2 {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-size: 22px;
        margin: 40px 0 8px;
      }

      .updated { color: var(--color-content-muted); margin: 0 0 40px; }

      /* The one claim a reader is most likely to be surprised by, so it is
         the one thing on the page given a surface of its own. */
      .callout {
        background: var(--color-surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        border-left: 3px solid var(--color-signal);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 16px 20px;
        margin: 24px 0;
      }

      table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 16px 0; }
      th, td {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 10px 12px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        vertical-align: top;
      }
      th { font-weight: 600; }
      td:first-child { white-space: nowrap; }

      footer {
        margin-top: 56px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        color: var(--color-content-muted);
        font-size: 15px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Help &amp; support</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        supermessage is made by Super Jackfruit Labs. If something is wrong — with the app, with
        your account, or with someone you met through it — this page is how to reach us.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>To report abuse, use the app first.</strong> Long-press the message and choose
        <em>Report…</em>, or open the room's info and tap a person to report or block them.
        Reports reach the administrators of your homeserver. On our homeserver,
        <code>id.agentpod.dev</code>, that is us, and <strong>we act on reports within 24
        hours</strong>.
      </div>

      <h2>Contact</h2>

      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:support@superjackfruit.com">support@superjackfruit.com</a>. A person
        reads it, and we reply within 24 hours. For privacy questions or to delete your account,
        see the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and
        <a href="/delete-account/">account deletion</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Reporting abuse</h2>

      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>What</th>
          <th>How</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>A message</td>
          <td>Long-press it and choose <em>Report…</em>. Add a reason if you can. The message is
            hidden from you as soon as the report is sent, and you can block its sender in the
            same step.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>A person or an agent</td>
          <td>Open the room's info, tap them, and choose <em>Report…</em> or <em>Block</em>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>A room or an invitation</td>
          <td>Open the room's info and choose <em>Report room…</em>, or tap <em>Report room…</em>
            under an invitation. You do not have to join a room to report it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Anything else</td>
          <td>Email <a href="mailto:support@superjackfruit.com">support@superjackfruit.com</a> with
            what happened and, if you can, the room and a screenshot.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <p>
        The person you report is not told who reported them. When a report is about content on
        our homeserver, we review it within 24 hours and remove content or deactivate accounts
        that break the <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Blocking</h2>

      <p>
        Blocking someone hides their messages from you in every room, on every device you are
        signed in on, and they are not told. You can block an agent the same way: its messages
        stop reaching you, and the agent itself keeps running for everyone else. Unblock anyone
        from <em>Account → Blocked</em>.
      </p>

      <h2>If you use another homeserver</h2>

      <p>
        supermessage can sign in to any Matrix homeserver. Reports made there go to whoever runs
        that server, under their rules and response times rather than ours. You can still email
        us about the app itself.
      </p>

      <footer>
        <a href="/">← supermessage</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms of use</a> ·
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
